# retired.list — files earlier OCBM versions placed that this version no longer ships. One path per
# line, relative to /, under usr/sbin, usr/bin or script (nothing else is ever deleted). Shipped as
# /etc/ocbm/retired.list in the image's payload and in every update package:
#   - ocbm_dispatch.sh's update_commit deletes them once an update has passed its self-test, so a
#     rollback still has them;
#   - once.sh deletes them when it installs over an earlier OCBM.
# Lines are only ever added. A path that comes back in a later version must leave this list first.
usr/sbin/aa-bridge
